settings-appearance-title = Appearance
settings-appearance-description = Pick Light or Dark, or let System follow Windows.
settings-minimizeToTray-title = Minimize to tray
settings-minimizeToTray-description = Closing the window sends Prune to the system tray instead of quitting.
settings-lowPowerMode-title = Low power mode
settings-lowPowerMode-description = Pauses the background animation, flattens the glass panels, and shortens transitions to near-instant. Turned on automatically at install if this PC looks like it would benefit; change it here anytime.
settings-updateCheck-title = Check for updates
settings-updateCheck-description = Once a day, Prune asks api.github.com whether a newer release exists. It is the only request Prune makes to anywhere but this machine, and GitHub sees your IP address as any website would. When there is one, an update button appears at the bottom of the side bar, and nothing is downloaded or installed until you click it.
settings-autoInstallUpdates-title = Install updates automatically
settings-autoInstallUpdates-description = Downloads a new version in the background and installs it the next time Prune closes, instead of waiting for you to click the update button. Needs the update check above.
settings-updateStatus-checking = Checking…
settings-updateStatus-loadError = Couldn't check for updates: { $error }
