settings-updateStatus-openDownloadPage = Open the download page
settings-updateStatus-upToDate = You're on the latest version ({ $version }).
settings-updateStatus-openPageError = Couldn't open the page: { $error }
settings-showFreeSpace-title = Show free space on the Disk Map
settings-showFreeSpace-description = Draws the drive's free space as one more block when you scan a whole drive, so every folder reads as a share of the drive rather than of the space in use.
settings-deepCleanRemoval-title = When Deep Clean removes files
settings-deepCleanRemoval-quarantine-label = Move to Quarantine (you can put it back)
settings-deepCleanRemoval-quarantine-description = Nothing is deleted. Files go into Prune's Quarantine and the drive gets the space back when you empty it.
settings-deepCleanRemoval-delete-label = Delete now (frees the space, can't be undone)
settings-deepCleanRemoval-delete-description = Files are removed as soon as you confirm, so the space is free straight away. Rules that lose data still ask first.
settings-deepCleanRemoval-deleteWarning = With Delete now, Clean can't be undone. Scheduled cleans still move files to Quarantine.
settings-deepCleanRemoval-autoQuarantineNote = Not used while Deep Clean deletes files immediately.
settings-autoQuarantine-title = Auto-Quarantine
settings-autoQuarantine-description = Deep Clean moves what it takes into Prune's Quarantine, where you can put it back. Turn this off and it goes to the Windows Recycle Bin instead — still recoverable, just somewhere you already know how to empty.
settings-skipRecent-title = Leave recent files alone
settings-skipRecent-description = Skip anything modified in the last few hours. In a temp folder a file being written right now looks exactly like one abandoned two years ago — this is what stops a half-finished install being swept up. 0 turns it off.
settings-skipRecent-hoursUnit = hours
settings-skipRecent-ariaLabel = Hours to leave recent files alone
settings-restorePointCleanup-title = Restore point before removing leftovers
settings-restorePointCleanup-description = Taken before Prune removes the leftover files and registry keys you selected, including after Force remove. On by default; does nothing at all if System Protection is turned off.
settings-hideUnavailable-title = Hide cleaners that don't apply
settings-hideUnavailable-description = Most of the list is for software this machine doesn't have. Hiding those leaves only what is actually here.
settings-quarantineRetention-title = How long to keep Quarantine items
settings-quarantineRetention-description = Everything Prune removes goes to Quarantine first, and stays until you empty it. Set a number of days to drop backups older than that. Leave it blank to keep them forever.
settings-quarantineRetention-neverPlaceholder = Never
settings-quarantineRetention-daysUnit = days
settings-quarantineRetention-ariaLabel = Days to keep quarantine backups
settings-quarantineMaxSize-title = Quarantine size limit
settings-quarantineMaxSize-description = A cap on the whole Quarantine folder. Over it, the oldest backups go first — the most recent one is never dropped, so something big you just removed stays recoverable even if it is larger than the cap on its own. Leave it blank for no limit.
settings-quarantineMaxSize-noLimitPlaceholder = No limit
settings-quarantineMaxSize-gbUnit = GB
settings-quarantineMaxSize-ariaLabel = Maximum quarantine size in gigabytes
settings-exclusions-title = Exclusions
settings-exclusions-description = Folders and file types Prune will leave alone — skipped by Deep Clean and left out of the Disk Map — on top of the ones it already protects: System Volume Information, antivirus quarantines, the component store and a dozen others. Folders and registry keys listed here are also never offered as leftovers after an uninstall.
settings-exclusions-ariaLabel = Folder path, file type or registry key to exclude
settings-exclusions-add = Add
settings-exclusions-invalidFormat = Write a full folder path (D:\Games), a file type (*.iso) or a registry key (HKCU\Software\Vendor).
settings-exclusions-formatHint = A full folder path, a file type written as *.iso, or a registry key such as HKCU\Software\Vendor
settings-exclusions-none = Nothing excluded.
settings-exclusions-typeBadge = Type
settings-exclusions-folderBadge = Folder
settings-exclusions-registryBadge = Registry
