settings-warningConfirmations-reset = Reset warning confirmations
settings-uninstallTab-beforeHeading = Before uninstalling
settings-uninstallTab-restorePointUninstall-title = Restore point before running an uninstaller
settings-uninstallTab-restorePointUninstall-description = Taken before the program's own uninstaller runs. It needs Prune to be running as administrator and Windows allows one a day, so when it can't be made the uninstall goes ahead and the dialog says so.
settings-uninstallTab-registryBackup-title = Back up the registry before uninstalling
settings-uninstallTab-registryBackup-description = Exports HKLM\SOFTWARE and HKCU\Software, typically several hundred MB, and keeps the newest 3. If the backup can't be made, the uninstall doesn't run.
settings-uninstallTab-deleteLockedFiles-title = Delete locked files on next restart
settings-uninstallTab-deleteLockedFiles-description = Files another program still has open are removed the next time you restart your computer, instead of only being reported as skipped. Needs administrator, or they're still just reported as skipped.
settings-uninstallTab-afterHeading = After uninstalling
settings-uninstallTab-scanLeftovers-title = Scan for leftovers after uninstalling
settings-uninstallTab-scanLeftovers-description = Looks for the files, registry keys and scheduled tasks the uninstaller left behind. Off, Prune runs the program's own uninstaller and stops there.
settings-uninstallTab-preselect-title = Tick every leftover by default
settings-uninstallTab-preselect-description = The review opens with everything it found ticked. Off, it opens with nothing ticked and you choose.
settings-uninstallTab-keepHistory-title = Keep an uninstall history
settings-uninstallTab-keepHistory-description = The dashboard's list of recent removals and the space they freed. Off, nothing new is recorded.
settings-uninstallTab-destinationHeading = Leftover files go to
settings-uninstallTab-leftoverOptions-quarantine-label = Quarantine
settings-uninstallTab-leftoverOptions-quarantine-description = Moved into Prune's own backup, and restorable from the Quarantine screen. The default.
settings-uninstallTab-leftoverOptions-recycle-label = The Recycle Bin
settings-uninstallTab-leftoverOptions-recycle-description = Restorable from Windows' own bin, and freed when you empty it.
settings-uninstallTab-leftoverOptions-permanent-label = Delete permanently
settings-uninstallTab-leftoverOptions-permanent-description = Deleted outright. Nothing to restore.
settings-uninstallTab-permanentWarning = Leftover files will be deleted outright and can't be restored, from Quarantine or anywhere else. Check the list before you confirm it.
settings-uninstallTab-registryNote = Registry keys are exported to Quarantine before they are removed, whichever you choose.
settings-about-reportTitle = Report a bug
settings-about-reportDescription = Opens a pre-filled issue on GitHub. Nothing is sent by Prune itself, and you see everything before it goes anywhere.
settings-about-reportButton = Report a bug
settings-about-description = A local, offline uninstaller and cleanup tool for Windows — forced removal with leftover-file scanning, safe quarantine-before-delete, disk mapping, and a cleaner that shows a preview before it removes anything.
settings-automation-title = Automation
settings-automation-description = Runs while Prune is open. It cannot wake a sleeping machine — a window that passes while the computer is off is reported as missed rather than silently skipped, and caught up the next time you open the app.
